<h2 id="common-whatsapp-api-message-sending-errors-and-solutions"><b>Common WhatsApp API Message Sending Errors and Solutions</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Sometimes messages fail to deliver even after setting up everything right. Here are some common reasons behind that: </span></p>
<h3 id="1-template-not-approved"><b>1. Template Not Approved</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You try to send messages, but it fails because Meta rejects your message template.</span></p>
<p><b>Common Reasons:  </b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Category mismatch</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Formatting errors, like variables placed at the start or end of the message</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Violation of WhatsApp policies</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Misleading content </span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Solution: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Check template status in your Meta Business Manager, fix any policy violation, and resubmit the template for approval. </span></p>
<h3 id="2-message-failed-to-deliver"><b>2. Message Failed to Deliver</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Sometimes messages are sent but never reach your customer. </span></p>
<p><b>Common reasons: </b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Invalid phone number </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Recipient blocked the number</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Network or connectivity issue</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Message limit restrictions</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Solution:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Re-verify the phone number, ensure the customer has not blocked you, and check your API account status. </span></p>
<h3 id="3-customer-not-opted-in"><b>3. Customer Not Opted-In</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Meta requires customer consent before sending any marketing or template messages.</span></p>
<p><b>Common reasons</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Contact added without consent</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">No customer permission collected</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Solution:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Always </span><a href="/resources/blog/ways-to-collect-whatsapp-opt-in/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">collect clear WhatsApp opt-ins from customers</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> before sending messages via forms, website checkouts, WhatsApp widgets, or other approved methods. </span></p>
<h3 id="4-quality-rating-issues"><b>4. Quality Rating Issues</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Meta regularly monitors how customers interact with your messages. Too many blocks or reports lead to lower quality ratings.</span></p>
<p><b>Common Reasons: </b></p>
<ul>
